  "title": "Add G_GNUC_ALLOC_SIZE annotations to wmem functions.",
  "description": "This Glib macro uses `__attribute__((alloc_size(n)))` to aid static analysis of\nbuffer bounds.  Using it on `wmem_alloc`, `wmem_alloc0`, `wmem_realloc` and\n`wmem_memdup` gives the compiler's static analyzer a chance to detect\nout-of-bounds accesses to the buffers they return.\n\nIt would be nice to extend this to some of the tvb functions, but the tvb API's\nuse of length -1 to indicate \"to the end of the tvbuff\" gets in the way.\n\nThis annotation surfaced the issue addressed in commit 54410038.",
